se to boston  also was hit very hard  now it's about who's testing  who has guidelines where are people  wearing masks etc  so now it's about policy cases  of course depend on tests and how much  testing you were doing  and as we know as i told you last week  florida and california as examples  were under reporting cases for different  reasons florida because of the hurricane  california  for still some unknown reason so when  you look at one of these examples let's  look at for example  florida because of the decreased testing  in florida  florida cases started declining in late  july  except we know why they aren't testing  as much because of the hurricane  but if you look instead of it cases at  hospitalizations during the last week  florida had a record for single week  new hospitalizations for coronavirus  just over 3 300 that's more than  500 new hospitalizations per day  including 621 hospitalizations  in florida last wednesday that's not  what you want to see and it's another  signal of how  you can affect cases by not testing by  changing reporting  hospitalizations are a really important  indicator now meanwhile  for political reasons donald trump is  talking about  every country now is seeing a resurgence  and the reason trump is doing this is if  he can point to  spain is having a wave too italy's  having a wave too  i guess he thinks it makes the united  states response look less  bad but there's a few really important  things to think about as we look at some  european countries  see numbers start to climb again first  of all we've been expecting a second  wave  since march this was what doctors  thought would happen  decrease in the summer back up as we  approach fall  in the u.s we never even had the gap  because when we got down to 20 000 cases  per day  most states started reopening which is  crazy  now to the other piece yes if you look  at  some european countries now like spain  they are seeing a resurgence in cases  but they're immediately putting the  guidelines back in place  and people are mostly following them so  when the president points to  we're doing fine because there are  second waves in europe well first  reaction is  we knew and expected all along that  there would be a second wave  in the u.s we've been so acutely  terrible that we didn't even get a break  from wave one to wave two and we're now  approaching the fall ourselves  secondly the other countries see the  rise  and they put the guidelines back in  place paris is now ramping back  up masking rules and putting measures  back in place trump points to spain and  france to justify  not having taken it seriously but the  problem with his logic is  they did take it seriously and  immediately are starting to right away  it's completely incoherent  but it's where we are today and all we  can do is deal with it  real quick uh august 23rd  is the 15-year anniversary of the david  pakman show this is a really big deal  we're on track for a million youtube  subscribers this year  our podcast has grown 40 percent in the  last three months  and we're hitting 15 years so on the  23rd  we will have a huge very special  membership special which you can be  notified of by grabbing a  free newsletter subscription at  davidpakman.com  this is very exciting we're doing  something crazy that i may even regret  some governors would probably call the  membership special we're planning  illegal and immoral i would even say but  we're going to persevere and do it so  get on our newsletter at davidpakman.com  august 23rd a big big day  in david pakman show history
 

